# Built docs examples (generated by build:docs)
docs/examples/
# Tool output that lands in the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY, not in the project it belongs to.
#
# `.playwright-mcp/` is created by the Playwright MCP server wherever its process was started, and a
# screenshot asked for by a bare filename lands in the same place — neither knows which project the
# work is for. A session whose cwd is this repo while it works on another game will drop that game's
# frames here. It has already happened once in this workspace: 110 screenshots from three unrelated
# projects went into gamelabs.toonblastmechanic's history in a single `git add -A`.
#
# Screenshots that are genuinely this project's evidence belong under a directory committed on
# purpose (assets/forge/), or in a scratch dir outside the repo.
.playwright-mcp/
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp